cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository in your research, please cite it as below. See also the paper 'Asymmetric Input Format Sensitivity in LLM-Based VNF Placement'."
title: "VNF LLM Sensitivity: Input Format Sensitivity in LLM-Based VNF Placement"
abstract: >-
  Experiments studying how the input representation format (edge list, adjacency matrix,
  natural language, JSON, ranked neighbor) affects Large Language Model reasoning on
  Virtual Network Function (VNF) placement, comparing GPT and DeepSeek against ILP-optimal
  solutions and greedy/random baselines.
